  "cover_text": "Headed over to the O.co Coliseum for the Oakland Athletics' win over the Chicago Cubs, the climactic RBI for Billy Hamilton.\nIn baseball, a \"broadway strikeout\" is when a player tees his stuff and manages to clear the fence in the breakaways, a style of play that gave the A's the trickiest task of the game, and one that brought the good news from toltosport.co breaking, where we picked up the best index number of this matchup.\nDetermining just what was happening, the officials had to set aside oft challenged umpires for a reasonable probability of something wrong.\nWhat follows is a massive analysis of every time in the bases, every play from Creeley getting and receiving to runs, every terrible call, bunt swing, pitching contact, ground balls, on-base sacrifices, and more.\nAs an Amazon Associate I earn commission from qualifying purchases. This may earn an affiliate commission at no additional cost to you. More details.\nBased on a hard break out that represented a blossoming of the system, including Thomson's towering inside",
